Built the generator, but it is not yet shippable because the required OpenRouter quota is exhausted.

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2011.08447/gen_2011_08447.py)
- [Local gate report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2011.08447/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2011.08447/README.md)
- [Failed oracle transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2011.08447/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)

The Track A family uses the paper’s native `r=t=0` ordinary planted-clique specialization, with `p=1/2` and `k≈1.1n^0.4`, below its polynomial-time recovery regime. This choice is supported by the paper’s Section 1.4 discussion and the cited SoS lower bound. [Paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2011.08447), [SoS lower bound](https://arxiv.org/abs/1604.03084).

Local results:

- G1–G8 pass.
- Random guessing: 0/200,000.
- Five attacks: each 0/8 successes.
- Exact search exhausted 100,000 nodes on all eight seeds.
- Answer: 65 characters, 16 elements.
- Intended route: 135 operations.

The hardening harness received HTTP 403 `Key limit exceeded (total limit)` on every redraw, so G9 remains pending and the hinted/placebo transcripts were not created. Restore the OpenRouter key’s quota, then rerun:

```bash
cd /home/gson/gvrepo/results/2011.08447
