codex
Rejected after reading the full paper.

- Theorem 2’s intended regime is polynomial-time solvable by SDP rounding, so it cannot support Track A.
- Track B also fails: the paper provides no compact route independent of solving the SDP.
- The below-threshold planted-clique fallback is plausibly hard, and five local attacks failed 0/8, but discovering the correct branch still required over 100,000 search nodes. Counting only the 135 operations after choosing that branch would assume the answer and violate G9(c).
- OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 quota errors; these were preserved but not treated as hardness evidence.

Artifacts:

- [REJECTED.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2011.08447/REJECTED.md)
- [rejected_gen_2011_08447.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2011.08447/rejected_gen_2011_08447.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2011.08447/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2011.08447/README.md)
- [hardening transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2011.08447/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)

The rejection records both the mechanical cost and missing compact-route length, with references to Definition 2, Theorem 2, and Algorithm 1 of the [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2011.08447).
